{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_20260614204326e059a306aa1b42c7","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The issue is that when models aren't registered in the test context, the createModelCall function will fail because it can't find the models. I need to make the defaultBuildSdkConfig more resilient - it should fall back to observe-only provider when the inference config isn't viable (when models aren't available).\n\nActually, looking at this more carefully, I think the better approach is to have defaultBuildSdkConfig check if inference is viable and fall back to observe-only provider if not. This way:\n1. Production path uses ModelCall when models are available\n2. Tests can still work with synthetic contexts that don't have models\n3. The fail-closed behavior is preserved when models aren't configured\n\nLet me update defaultBuildSdkConfig to handle this gracefully:","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7894f3ec-841a-4c17-b9cf-403440004aac","uuid":"b7ad306c-3b5a-418e-acb8-0a1ed7c2220a"}
